From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gino (WLTB-Gino) <gino@wltechblog.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Nov 2026 01:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] motor: make remove() teardown safe against IRQs and timers

motor_remove() tore things down in an order that leaves windows for
use-after-free / NULL-deref on module unload and reload:

- del_timer_sync() ran after gpio_free() and after motor->pdata = 0,
  so an already-armed min/max debounce timer (armed from the GPIO
  hardirq, firing 5ms later from softirq) could dereference the
  released pdata.
- mutex_destroy() and ingenic_tcu_counter_stop() ran while /dev/motor
  was still registered and the procfs entry was still mounted, so a
  racing open/ioctl or proc reader could take a mutex that is being
  destroyed or drive a TCU channel that is being stopped.

Order now: free all IRQs first (no new timer arms can happen), drain
the debounce timers while pdata is still valid, drop pdata, remove
the procfs entry and /dev/motor, and only then destroy the mutex and
stop the TCU counter.

Companion to 0005 (devres double-free); together they close the
teardown races seen around runtime motor.ko reload on noorio t110.

Signed-off-by: Gino (WLTB-Gino) <gino@wltechblog.com>
--- a/common/misc/motor/motor.c
+++ b/common/misc/motor/motor.c
@@ -1004,9 +1004,6 @@
 	int i;
 	struct motor_device *mdev = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	struct motor_driver *motor = NULL;
-	ingenic_tcu_counter_stop(mdev->tcu);
-	mutex_destroy(&mdev->dev_mutex);
-
 	free_irq(mdev->run_step_irq, mdev);
 	for(i = 0; i < HAS_MOTOR_CNT; i++) {
 		motor = &(mdev->motors[i]);
@@ -1031,13 +1028,14 @@
 
 		if (motor->pdata->motor_st4_gpio != -1)
 			gpio_free(motor->pdata->motor_st4_gpio);
+		/* phase gone, no more phases will be armed */
+		del_timer_sync(&motor->min_timer);
+		del_timer_sync(&motor->max_timer);
 		motor->pdata = 0;
 		motor->min_pos_irq = 0;
 		motor->max_pos_irq = 0;
 		motor->min_pos_irq_cnt = 0;
 		motor->max_pos_irq_cnt = 0;
-		del_timer_sync(&motor->min_timer);
-		del_timer_sync(&motor->max_timer);
 	}
 
 	if (mdev->proc)
@@ -1045,6 +1043,16 @@
 
 	misc_deregister(&mdev->misc_dev);
 
+	/*
+	 * Userspace is gone and every callback touching mdev has been
+	 * stopped: tear down the mutex and TCU channel after the device
+	 * entry points are removed, so nothing can dereference them while
+	 * they are being released.
+	 */
+	mutex_destroy(&mdev->dev_mutex);
+
+	ingenic_tcu_counter_stop(mdev->tcu);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
